  "prompt_rules": [
    "Spelling is UN/UK English: -ize endings (organize, prioritize, recognize) but -our (colour, labour, favour), -re (centre, metre, litre) and a double l (travelled, cancelled, fuelled, labelled).",
    "Numbers one to nine are written as words; use numerals for 10 and above. Never start a sentence with a numeral. Always write 'per cent' as two words, with the number as a numeral (5 per cent) — no % symbol in running text.",
    "Dates are day month year, no commas and no ordinal suffixes: 19 August 2026, not August 19th 2026.",
    "No serial (Oxford) comma: 'Governments, donors and aid agencies'.",
    "Upper-case Government when it means the Government of a State; lower case for a local or municipal government, a system of government, or government officials. Same for State: upper case only inside an official name.",
    "Currency: US$ on first mention, $ after, with no space before the number. Always add 'million' or 'billion' where relevant.",
    "Prefer the active voice. Prefer 'people' to 'beneficiaries', 'populations' or 'individuals'. Use 'who', not 'that', for people, and 'such as', not 'like', for comparisons.",
    "Avoid jargon. Say what actually happened rather than 'humanitarian consequences' or 'capacity to respond'.",
    "Never reword the speaker. These rules govern any text YOU write back to me — they are not licence to edit the quoted transcript beyond spelling and capitalization."
  ]
